QModem pages: request values reach the shell quoted

The LuCI controller built its shell commands by pasting request values into them. In
modemCtrl, the action and the modem section name went in unquoted and params inside double
quotes, where the shell still expands $(...), backticks and $VAR; sendATCommand pasted the AT
port and command in unquoted. Any value with a space broke the request (an AT command such as
AT+QCFG="band", 0 lost everything after the space), and a crafted value ran as a shell command
as root. The pages need a logged-in administrator, so this was not reachable from outside, but
it turned a page form into a root shell and broke ordinary input.

- controller/qmodem.lua: every request value goes to the shell single-quoted (shq). The action
  and the section name must be letters, digits, _ and - only, or the request gets a 400. The
  pages send params JSON-encoded one level more than the script reads; the double quotes used
  to strip that level by accident, so it is now taken off explicitly (a params value that
  parses as a JSON string is replaced by that string). Every existing caller - Lock Band, Rat
  Prefer, Dial Mode, Set IMEI, Neighbor Cell, Reboot Modem, AT Debug - sends exactly what it
  sent before to the script.
- modem_ctrl.sh: "$3" is quoted where it is handed to set_imei, set_lockband, set_mode,
  set_neighborcell, set_network_prefer, set_sms_storage and set_sim_slot, and in the reboot,
  send_at and send_sms branches, so a value keeps its spaces and a * in it is not a glob.

Applies to: https://github.com/FUjr/QModem.git @ 0988085b, after 0012.
Upstream status: local to CleanWRT.

--- a/luci/luci-app-qmodem/luasrc/controller/qmodem.lua
+++ b/luci/luci-app-qmodem/luasrc/controller/qmodem.lua
@@ -9,6 +9,17 @@
 local run_path="/tmp/run/qmodem/"
 local modem_ctrl = "/usr/share/qmodem/modem_ctrl.sh "
 
+-- CleanWRT: values from a request reach the shell single-quoted, so spaces,
+-- quotes, $ and backticks in them are data, never shell syntax
+local function shq(s)
+	return "'" .. (tostring(s or ""):gsub("'", "'\\''")) .. "'"
+end
+
+-- an action or a modem section name: letters, digits, _ and - only
+local function is_name(s)
+	return type(s) == "string" and s:match("^[%w_%-]+$") ~= nil
+end
+
 function index()
     if not nixio.fs.access("/etc/config/qmodem") then
         return
@@ -72,10 +83,26 @@
 	local cfg_id = http.formvalue("cfg")
 	local params = http.formvalue("params")
 	local translate = http.formvalue("translate")
+	-- CleanWRT: the action and the section name were pasted into the command
+	-- unquoted, and params inside double quotes, where the shell still expands
+	-- $(...), backticks and $VAR. Refuse a malformed name; quote every value.
+	if not is_name(action) or not is_name(cfg_id) then
+		luci.http.status(400, "Bad Request")
+		luci.http.prepare_content("application/json")
+		luci.http.write('{"error":"invalid action or cfg"}')
+		return
+	end
 	if params then
-		result = shell(modem_ctrl..action.." "..cfg_id.." ".."\""..params.."\"")
-	else 
-		result = shell(modem_ctrl..action.." "..cfg_id)
+		-- The pages send params JSON-encoded one level more than the script
+		-- reads (a JSON string holding the JSON). The double quotes used to strip
+		-- that level as a side effect; take it off here instead.
+		local inner = json.parse(params)
+		if type(inner) == "string" then
+			params = inner
+		end
+		result = shell(modem_ctrl..shq(action).." "..shq(cfg_id).." "..shq(params))
+	else
+		result = shell(modem_ctrl..shq(action).." "..shq(cfg_id))
 	end
 	if translate == "1" then
 		modem_more_info = json.parse(result)
@@ -93,7 +120,8 @@
 	at_command AT命令
 ]]
 function at(at_port,at_command)
-	local command="source "..script_path.."modem_util.sh && at "..at_port.." "..at_command
+	-- CleanWRT: the port and the command are request values: quote them
+	local command="source "..script_path.."modem_util.sh && at "..shq(at_port).." "..shq(at_command)
 	local result=shell(command)
 	result=string.gsub(result, "\r", "")
 	return result
